{"Success":true,"Data":{"State":"open","OpenTime":0,"CloseTime":0,"IsApproved":true,"IsPinned":false,"IsDeleted":false,"IsHidden":false,"IsArchived":false,"IsFollowing":false,"CanEdit":false,"CanReply":true,"CanFollow":true,"TotalPosts":10,"QueuedPosts":0,"DeletedPosts":0,"HasUnreadPosts":false,"HasAttachments":true,"Views":634,"MovedTo":null,"MovedOn":0,"FirstPostId":1897167,"Rating":0,"RatingHits":0,"Starter":{"Id":277044,"Name":"smileitseb","Photo":{"HasPhoto":true,"PhotoUrl":"http:\/\/bdw.stevewright.netdna-cdn.com\/cdn\/profile\/photo-277044.jpg?_r=1432531828","PhotoWidth":200,"PhotoHeight":241,"PhotoType":"custom"},"IsOnline":false},"StartDate":1432513475,"LastPoster":{"Id":282132,"Name":"KatieMcBride","Photo":{"HasPhoto":true,"PhotoUrl":"http:\/\/bdw.stevewright.netdna-cdn.com\/cdn\/profile\/photo-282132.jpg?_r=1437519508","PhotoWidth":200,"PhotoHeight":200,"PhotoType":"facebook"},"IsOnline":false},"PollState":"0","LastVote":0,"ForumId":37,"Preview":{"Id":1897167,"PostDate":1432513475,"PostContent":"My Dream Wedding at Dreams Riviera Cancun (Dreams of Love Package \u2013 58 guests) \u00a0 Wedding Coordina...","Author":{"Signature":"<p>58 guests plus bride and groom<br>\nCeremony: Gazebo<br>\nReception: Pool Deck","Email":"smileitseb@gmail.com","IpAddress":"50.90.104.129","GroupId":40,"GroupName":"Jr. Member","JoinDate":1394205869,"Photo":{"HasPhoto":true,"PhotoUrl":"http:\/\/bdw.stevewright.netdna-cdn.com\/cdn\/profile\/photo-277044.jpg?_r=1432531828","PhotoWidth":200,"PhotoHeight":241,"PhotoType":"custom"},"FormattedName":"smileitseb","Id":277044,"Name":"smileitseb","IsOnline":false}},"Posts":[{"Title":null,"ShowSignature":true,"ShowEmoticons":true,"IpAddress":"50.90.101.224","IsFirstPost":true,"IsQueued":false,"IsVisible":true,"IsDeleted":false,"CanEdit":false,"CanDelete":false,"CanLike":true,"TopicId":79211,"EditedBy":"","EditDate":0,"EditReason":"","DeleteDate":0,"TotalLikes":7,"IsLiked":false,"PostKey":"51ce3c8cb41d935410fe7b34371f9d41","RawContent":"&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=\"font-family:arial, sans-serif;\"&gt;&lt;span style=\"font-size:9pt;\"&gt;My Dream Wedding at Dreams Riviera Cancun (Dreams of Love Package \u2013 58 guests)&lt;\/span&gt;&lt;\/span&gt;&lt;\/p&gt;\n&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;\/p&gt;\n&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;span style=\"font-family:arial, sans-serif;\"&gt;&lt;span style=\"font-size:9pt;\"&gt;Wedding Coordinator:&lt;\/span&gt;&lt;\/span&gt;&lt;\/strong&gt;&lt;span style=\"font-family:arial, sans-serif;\"&gt;&lt;span style=\"font-size:9pt;\"&gt; A+++++++ --My wedding coordinator, Elisa Guadarrama, was absolutely amazing. She began working with me about 4 months before my wedding and was usually very responsive (usually responding within 3 days or so). I know some brides want immediate responses but you have to understand that she is working with several other brides (some of whose weddings are approaching before yours), coordinating weddings real-time, waiting on responses from vendors, and also is not at work every day of the week so I thought the 3 day timeframe was reasonable. When I was checking in, she came to meet me and gave me the biggest hug and smile. As a southerner and avid hugger, it made me feel at ease. In our meeting, we went over every single detail of my wedding and welcome reception. I had planned to print out all of our email correspondence but it was going to be a ton of pages because we changed over 100 emails since January and it turns out that I didn\u2019t need it! We went through the wedding planner form, then the budget spreadsheet then just other random extras that weren\u2019t on either of those. We also went through the things I brought from home. I was very clear on our budget and that I couldn\u2019t go over it but that I wanted it to be very classy, very glam, and very colorful with my colors throughout. She made things work and in the end, I got EVERYTHING I wanted and even a few surprises that I didn\u2019t know she was throwing in. ;) She executed my vision of colorful glam perfectly. She is amazing and I would choose her over and over again.&lt;\/span&gt;&lt;\/span&gt;&lt;\/p&gt;\n&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;\/p&gt;\n&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;span style=\"font-family:arial, sans-serif;\"&gt;&lt;span style=\"font-size:9pt;\"&gt;Resort:&lt;\/span&gt;&lt;\/span&gt;&lt;\/strong&gt;&lt;span style=\"font-family:arial, sans-serif;\"&gt;&lt;span style=\"font-size:9pt;\"&gt; A+ --We really loved Dreams. It was beautiful. The rooms, the food, the lobby, the beach, pools, activities. We loved it all. We were pampered from the moment we walked in with the champagne and cold towels. We were there the weekend of the Mayweather-Pacquiao fight and Dreams planned a fight event where everyone could watch it on 3 large screens. None of my guests wanted to miss the fight and it gave them something to do Saturday night after dinner so it was perfect. There were a lot of special touches, excellent service, and other great things that made me feel great about our choice in Dreams. I did not have the privilege to do the site visit beforehand, but I can say it was better in person than all the pictures and reviews I obsessed over for months. &lt;\/span&gt;&lt;\/span&gt;&lt;\/p&gt;\n&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;\/p&gt;\n&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;span style=\"font-family:arial, sans-serif;\"&gt;&lt;span style=\"font-size:9pt;\"&gt;Room:&lt;\/span&gt;&lt;\/span&gt;&lt;\/strong&gt;&lt;span style=\"font-family:arial, sans-serif;\"&gt;&lt;span style=\"font-size:9pt;\"&gt; A+ --Me and my mom booked the Preferred Club Master Suite. Then, my husband stayed there wedding night. (he stayed in an ocean view room for the nights before the wedding\u2014I\u2019m super traditional &lt;\/span&gt;&lt;\/span&gt;&lt;span style=\"font-family:wingdings;\"&gt;&lt;span style=\"font-size:9pt;\"&gt;J&lt;\/span&gt;&lt;\/span&gt;&lt;span style=\"font-family:arial, sans-serif;\"&gt;&lt;span style=\"font-size:9pt;\"&gt;). Ladies, the Master Suite was expensive yes BUT, I am so happy we booked it. We used the value of the free rooms (book 5 get a 6&lt;sup&gt;th&lt;\/sup&gt; free) we received to pay for it. On Friday night, my bridesmaids threw me a bachelorette party in our room before going out and with all 20 girls playing games, we definitely needed the space. Also, on our wedding day, with the photographers, videographers, my 4 bridesmaids, my mom, my backup makeup artist, my hair stylist \u2013 we really needed the space! I felt so comfortable. Plus, having that amazing view for the weekend was great, and I really think I deserved it after all the planning and stress!&lt;\/span&gt;&lt;\/span&gt;&lt;\/p&gt;\n&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;\/p&gt;\n&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;span style=\"font-family:arial, sans-serif;\"&gt;&lt;span style=\"font-size:9pt;\"&gt;Rehearsal:&lt;\/span&gt;&lt;\/span&gt;&lt;\/strong&gt;&lt;span style=\"font-family:arial, sans-serif;\"&gt;&lt;span style=\"font-size:9pt;\"&gt; Our rehearsal was scheduled at 10am Saturday morning. I was on time and so was my coordinator but we were missing the GROOM and half of the wedding party. My wedding coordinator asked could we move it to 11 when they still were not there by 10:10. Had my first (and only, thankfully) bridezilla moment because I was furious that they were not on time. But so thankful my WC was available for reschedule. I blamed it on our crazy partying in Cancun the night before and asked them to please be on time for the rest of the wedding events. &lt;\/span&gt;&lt;\/span&gt;&lt;\/p&gt;\n&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;\/p&gt;\n&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;span style=\"font-family:arial, sans-serif;\"&gt;&lt;span style=\"font-size:9pt;\"&gt;Welcome Reception:&lt;\/span&gt;&lt;\/span&gt;&lt;\/strong&gt;&lt;span style=\"font-family:arial, sans-serif;\"&gt;&lt;span style=\"font-size:9pt;\"&gt; We had our welcome reception Friday at 7pm at the North Jacuzzi. I had my guests all wear white and it turned out PERFECTLY. Elisa surprised me with lighting and signature drinks which matched my wedding colors called Purple Rain. She\u2019s such a doll. We handed out our welcome bags at the welcome reception and everyone mixed and mingled. &lt;\/span&gt;&lt;\/span&gt;&lt;span style=\"font-family:wingdings;\"&gt;&lt;span style=\"font-size:9pt;\"&gt;J&lt;\/span&gt;&lt;\/span&gt;&lt;span style=\"font-family:arial, sans-serif;\"&gt;&lt;span style=\"font-size:9pt;\"&gt; Appetizers: &lt;span style=\"color:rgb(40,40,40);\"&gt;roasted pepper and parmesan panini, shrimp satay, stuffed mushrooms, fish croquette, and spring rolls&lt;\/span&gt;&lt;\/span&gt;&lt;\/span&gt;&lt;\/p&gt;\n&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;\/p&gt;\n&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;span style=\"font-family:arial, sans-serif;\"&gt;&lt;span style=\"font-size:9pt;\"&gt;Flowers:&lt;\/span&gt;&lt;\/span&gt;&lt;\/strong&gt;&lt;span style=\"font-family:arial, sans-serif;\"&gt;&lt;span style=\"font-size:9pt;\"&gt; I love flowers and was insistent that there will be absolutely no fake flowers at my wedding and I\u2019m so happy with the result. Loved my cascading bouquet and my bridesmaid\u2019s bouquets, our centerpieces and the flower vases at the ceremony. I had fuchsia roses, purple orchids and purple lisianthus. Beautiful and vibrant colors just like I wanted.&lt;\/span&gt;&lt;\/span&gt;&lt;\/p&gt;\n&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;\/p&gt;\n&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;span style=\"font-family:arial, sans-serif;\"&gt;&lt;span style=\"font-size:9pt;\"&gt;Wedding Ceremony:&lt;\/span&gt;&lt;\/span&gt;&lt;\/strong&gt;&lt;span style=\"font-family:arial, sans-serif;\"&gt;&lt;span style=\"font-size:9pt;\"&gt; We had the symbolic ceremony at the gazebo at 5pm Sunday, May 3, 2015. I had been so nervous about it being so close to the pool and the onlookers but I did not notice anyone but my guests and groom. Now, looking at the pictures from my guests, I see there were a LOT of people watching from the pool and their balconies. Thankfully my photographers did not capture them in a lot of the pictures. It was BEAUTIFUL. I did not want to get married on sand because I love wearing heels and knew my now husband wanted to wear shoes too. Overlooking the ocean was just absolutely breathtaking. Elisa surprised me with the chandelier and drapery which looked amazing. Everything we had went over, from the flower vases, rose petals in aisle, chair sashes tied on the silver tiffany chairs, fans, reserved seating name tags \u2013 was executed perfectly. Better than I imagined. I love how all our pictures look and it felt magical. Our officiant was Luis Armando&amp;nbsp;Sanchez&amp;nbsp;Navarrete. I met with him on Saturday to go over the script I wrote and our name pronunciations. Very sweet man. Also very gracious, considering I was late for our appointment the day before. He did great but I will say I could not understand about 20% of the ceremony due to his heavy accent, but it was totally fine &lt;\/span&gt;&lt;\/span&gt;&lt;span style=\"font-family:wingdings;\"&gt;&lt;span style=\"font-size:9pt;\"&gt;J&lt;\/span&gt;&lt;\/span&gt;&lt;span style=\"font-family:arial, sans-serif;\"&gt;&lt;span style=\"font-size:9pt;\"&gt; I completely customized the ceremony script, did not have a sand ceremony, and we said our own vows. It was a very sweet ceremony.&lt;\/span&gt;&lt;\/span&gt;&lt;\/p&gt;\n&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;\/p&gt;\n&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;span style=\"font-family:arial, sans-serif;\"&gt;&lt;span style=\"font-size:9pt;\"&gt;Informal Cocktail Hour:&lt;\/span&gt;&lt;\/span&gt;&lt;\/strong&gt;&lt;span style=\"font-family:arial, sans-serif;\"&gt;&lt;span style=\"font-size:9pt;\"&gt; We opted to use the money included in the package for the 20 guests for the cocktail hour to extend our reception by 1 hour. So happy we did this. Our guests went to the lobby bar while we took pictures and it turned out great. &lt;\/span&gt;&lt;\/span&gt;&lt;\/p&gt;\n&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;\/p&gt;\n&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;span style=\"font-family:arial, sans-serif;\"&gt;&lt;span style=\"font-size:9pt;\"&gt;Wedding Reception:&lt;\/span&gt;&lt;\/span&gt;&lt;\/strong&gt;&lt;span style=\"font-family:arial, sans-serif;\"&gt;&lt;span style=\"font-size:9pt;\"&gt; MY FAVE. Our reception was on the pool deck from 7pm-11pm. I had 2 long empire tables and we sat at the sweetheart table. I upgraded the tablecloths to purple satin and our sweetheart table cloth to silver sequin. We also upgraded to the love seat for our sweetheart table. We had several beautiful flower arrangements, tall glass vases with floating candles, votive candle holders (with LED lights&lt;\/span&gt;&lt;\/span&gt;&lt;span style=\"font-family:wingdings;\"&gt;&lt;span style=\"font-size:9pt;\"&gt;J&lt;\/span&gt;&lt;\/span&gt;&lt;span style=\"font-family:arial, sans-serif;\"&gt;&lt;span style=\"font-size:9pt;\"&gt;), and mirrors under the vases down the center of each long empire table. I had exact seating arrangements, with a name tag on each maraca (which also tripled as our wedding favor and exit) that was placed directly on their napkin. For lighting, we had 2 strings of 20 floating lanterns. The bridal party entered the reception to Treasure by Bruno Mars. We then had our first dance to our guests holding sparklers, which I loveddddddddd. They only lasted a couple minutes but it was fine because we got great pictures and video while they did last. We had a combination of all the buffets, it was delicious. My guests said it was the best they had all weekend. We had the marble cake with orchids decorating and brought our own cake topper. For our guest book, we had a Polaroid camera where guests could take pictures with props and then sign a message under their picture. We made our own dinner playlist using our favorite love songs on Spotify. I did not want to rent the DJ because I did not think he would play all the songs we wanted, so we just had a mix made by a local DJ that we played through our iPad. We did not rent a dance floor but instead danced directly on the deck. We partied!!!!! My guests are so much fun and we didn\u2019t sit down the entire reception. We exited to everyone shaking their maracas and we danced down the middle. PERFECTION. Buffet: pasta salad, mixed greens with vegetables, chicken caesar salad, potato salad with scallions, homemade bread and rolls, seafood salad, cajun roasted potatoes, creole pasta, corn on the cob, chicken breast stuffed with spinach, seafood casserole, jamaican chicken, cajun beef brochettes, seafood paella, BBQ pork ribs, coconut and rum cake, brownies, carrot cake, apple strudel&lt;\/span&gt;&lt;\/span&gt;&lt;\/p&gt;\n&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;span style=\"font-family:arial, sans-serif;\"&gt;&lt;span style=\"font-size:9pt;\"&gt;After the wedding reception:&lt;\/span&gt;&lt;\/span&gt;&lt;\/strong&gt;&lt;span style=\"font-family:arial, sans-serif;\"&gt;&lt;span style=\"font-size:9pt;\"&gt; Never ever ever thought I would be a bride to continue partying with the guests after the reception was over but we really didn\u2019t want the night to end. I changed out of my dress into a cute little white outfit (had to stay looking bridal haha) and we headed down to the Desires Nightclub until 1am. We had SO MUCH FUN. And the DJ played whatever we wanted. It was perfect.&lt;\/span&gt;&lt;\/span&gt;&lt;\/p&gt;\n&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;\/p&gt;\n&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;span style=\"font-family:arial, sans-serif;\"&gt;&lt;span style=\"font-size:9pt;\"&gt;Farewell Brunch:&lt;\/span&gt;&lt;\/span&gt;&lt;\/strong&gt;&lt;span style=\"font-family:arial, sans-serif;\"&gt;&lt;span style=\"font-size:9pt;\"&gt; Most of our guests were leaving Monday so we had an informal brunch at the World Caf\u00e9 9:30am-11am. Mostly everyone came and some of our guests had gotten there early to save us a few tables. It was so great to hug and kiss everyone goodbye before we went to our amazing honeymoon (at Excellence Playa Mujeres \u2013 separate review on Trip Advisor). &lt;\/span&gt;&lt;\/span&gt;&lt;\/p&gt;\n&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;\/p&gt;\n&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;span style=\"font-family:arial, sans-serif;\"&gt;&lt;span style=\"font-size:9pt;\"&gt;Photographer\/Videographer:&lt;\/span&gt;&lt;\/span&gt;&lt;\/strong&gt;&lt;span style=\"font-family:arial, sans-serif;\"&gt;&lt;span style=\"font-size:9pt;\"&gt; B --Digital Cinema. So I did not have a lot of money for photography. I knew I wouldn\u2019t be spending the $5k plus like other brides even though I LOVE pictures. Thankfully, I found these guys by searching the #dreamsrivieracancun hashtag on Instagram and finding this beautiful brides pictures. I LOVE my pictures and love my highlight video. The communication was great at first, sometimes lacking but in the end I got a great price. I believe because of the language barriers, at times I do not think they understood some of my requests \u2013 specifically, about a week before my wedding I decided to extend my reception to 11pm instead of 10pm. I emailed them to ask the price to extend the reception to 11, they said $100, I said great let\u2019s do it, they said okay and also they will arrive at 3 instead of 4 (my ceremony started at 5). Fast forward to 10pm at my reception, they said they are leaving because they got there at 3 and that was the amount of hours we agreed on in our initial contract.&amp;nbsp; I was really upset for a few moments because I knew for a fact I was very specific in my emails but then decided not to argue with them. And plus I didn\u2019t have my phone to pull up my email to prove we agreed they were supposed to leave at 11 so I just let it go and decided to enjoy the rest of my reception. The only thing they didn\u2019t capture was the maraca exit but thankfully I have other footage of that. There were a few other issues of things I thought I should have received based on the contract, and I\u2019m still waiting to see if I will :\/ Also, there are shots I wish I would have gotten but I do love all the pics and video that we did receive so I\u2019m not going stress out about it.&lt;\/span&gt;&lt;\/span&gt;&lt;\/p&gt;\n&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;\/p&gt;\n&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;span style=\"font-family:arial, sans-serif;\"&gt;&lt;span style=\"font-size:9pt;\"&gt;Wedding Favors:&lt;\/span&gt;&lt;\/span&gt;&lt;\/strong&gt;&lt;span style=\"font-family:arial, sans-serif;\"&gt;&lt;span style=\"font-size:9pt;\"&gt; A --We ordered our personalized authentic maracas from Maracas Mexico. Communication was great and timely. The maracas were pretty and they were at the resort when I arrived. I ordered the original multicolor design and requested as many purple maracas as possible, which they agreed to. The only \u201ccomplaint\u201d I have is that I didn\u2019t receive not 1 purple maraca! But it actually turned out fine, it didn\u2019t matter &lt;\/span&gt;&lt;\/span&gt;&lt;span style=\"font-family:wingdings;\"&gt;&lt;span style=\"font-size:9pt;\"&gt;J&lt;\/span&gt;&lt;\/span&gt;&lt;\/p&gt;\n&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;\/p&gt;\n&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;span style=\"font-family:arial, sans-serif;\"&gt;&lt;span style=\"font-size:9pt;\"&gt;Welcome Bags:&lt;\/span&gt;&lt;\/span&gt;&lt;\/strong&gt;&lt;span style=\"font-family:arial, sans-serif;\"&gt;&lt;span style=\"font-size:9pt;\"&gt; I had paper welcome bags that I gave to everyone at our welcome reception that included tumblers from DollarTree with personalized stickers from Davet Designs, advil, hand sanitizer, bug repellent wipes, maraca keychains, welcome letter\/itinerary\/meet-the-guests booklet, and sunscreen. Only a few people used the tumblers, and even me and my now husband didn\u2019t use them because I would forget to take them down with us to the beach\/pool everyday lol. But oh well, it was another take home gift for our guests &lt;\/span&gt;&lt;\/span&gt;&lt;span style=\"font-family:wingdings;\"&gt;&lt;span style=\"font-size:9pt;\"&gt;J&lt;\/span&gt;&lt;\/span&gt;&lt;span style=\"font-family:arial, sans-serif;\"&gt;&lt;span style=\"font-size:9pt;\"&gt; People did love our booklets and said they used the advil, especially after our night partying in Cancun on Friday.&lt;\/span&gt;&lt;\/span&gt;&lt;\/p&gt;\n&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;\/p&gt;\n&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;span style=\"font-family:arial, sans-serif;\"&gt;&lt;span style=\"font-size:9pt;\"&gt;Makeup:&lt;\/span&gt;&lt;\/span&gt;&lt;\/strong&gt;&lt;span style=\"font-family:arial, sans-serif;\"&gt;&lt;span style=\"font-size:9pt;\"&gt; A --I had my makeup done at the spa at the resort by Concepcion. I was very nervous about the makeup so I bought all the makeup beforehand for my dream look and had my girls ready just in case I hated what the makeup lady did. Concepcion did AMAZING. I was very happy and I\u2019m very picky lol. She used all MAC products. She did use my foundation because I wanted a perfect match. She didn\u2019t have the exact lip color I wanted so I used my own lipstain\/gloss and polish that I brought. Very satisfied. As a side note, lashes are an additional $15 but I brought my own and had my friend put them on for me.&lt;\/span&gt;&lt;\/span&gt;&lt;\/p&gt;\n&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;\/p&gt;\n&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;span style=\"font-family:arial, sans-serif;\"&gt;&lt;span style=\"font-size:9pt;\"&gt;Hair:&lt;\/span&gt;&lt;\/span&gt;&lt;\/strong&gt;&lt;span style=\"font-family:arial, sans-serif;\"&gt;&lt;span style=\"font-size:9pt;\"&gt; I brought my own stylist.&lt;\/span&gt;&lt;\/span&gt;&lt;\/p&gt;\n&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;\/p&gt;\n&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=\"font-family:arial, sans-serif;\"&gt;&lt;span style=\"font-size:9pt;\"&gt;All in all, I HAD THE ABSOLUTE WEDDING OF MY DREAMS. I would not change a thing. A lot of my guests said it\u2019s the best wedding they have ever been to, and seeing all their smiles in the pictures and videos, makes me feel very happy. It was worth all the money and stress! Best day of my life. Complete fairytale.&lt;\/span&gt;&lt;\/span&gt;&lt;\/p&gt;\n&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;\/p&gt;\n&lt;p&gt;&lt;a data-ipb=&#039;nomediaparse&#039; href=&#039;https:\/\/vimeo.com\/128508480&#039;&gt;https:\/\/&lt;span&gt;vimeo&lt;\/span&gt;.com\/128508480&lt;\/a&gt;&lt;\/p&gt;\n&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;\/p&gt;\n&lt;p&gt;&lt;\/p&gt;\n&lt;div&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;\/div&gt;","Attachments":[],"Id":1897167,"PostDate":1432513475,"PostContent":"            <html>\r\n              <head>\r\n                <style type=\"\"text\/css\"\">\r\n                  body {\r\n                    font-size: 16px;\r\n                    font-family: Helvetica, Verdana;\r\n                  }\r\n                  img .bbc_img {\r\n                    width: 100%;\r\n                  }\r\n                <\/style>\r\n              <\/head>\r\n              <body>\r\n                <p><span  style=\"font-family:arial, sans-serif\"><span  style=\"font-size:9pt\">My Dream Wedding at Dreams Riviera Cancun (Dreams of Love Package \u2013 58 guests)<\/span><\/span><\/p>\n<p>\u00a0<\/p>\n<p><strong><span  style=\"font-family:arial, sans-serif\"><span  style=\"font-size:9pt\">Wedding Coordinator:<\/span><\/span><\/strong><span  style=\"font-family:arial, sans-serif\"><span  style=\"font-size:9pt\"> A+++++++ --My wedding coordinator, Elisa Guadarrama, was absolutely amazing. She began working with me about 4 months before my wedding and was usually very responsive (usually responding within 3 days or so). I know some brides want immediate responses but you have to understand that she is working with several other brides (some of whose weddings are approaching before yours), coordinating weddings real-time, waiting on responses from vendors, and also is not at work every day of the week so I thought the 3 day timeframe was reasonable. When I was checking in, she came to meet me and gave me the biggest hug and smile. As a southerner and avid hugger, it made me feel at ease. In our meeting, we went over every single detail of my wedding and welcome reception. I had planned to print out all of our email correspondence but it was going to be a ton of pages because we changed over 100 emails since January and it turns out that I didn\u2019t need it! We went through the wedding planner form, then the budget spreadsheet then just other random extras that weren\u2019t on either of those. We also went through the things I brought from home. I was very clear on our budget and that I couldn\u2019t go over it but that I wanted it to be very classy, very glam, and very colorful with my colors throughout. She made things work and in the end, I got EVERYTHING I wanted and even a few surprises that I didn\u2019t know she was throwing in. <img src='http:\/\/bdw.stevewright.netdna-cdn.com\/public\/style_emoticons\/default\/wink.png' class='bbc_emoticon' alt=';)' \/> She executed my vision of colorful glam perfectly. She is amazing and I would choose her over and over again.<\/span><\/span><\/p>\n<p>\u00a0<\/p>\n<p><strong><span  style=\"font-family:arial, sans-serif\"><span  style=\"font-size:9pt\">Resort:<\/span><\/span><\/strong><span  style=\"font-family:arial, sans-serif\"><span  style=\"font-size:9pt\"> A+ --We really loved Dreams. It was beautiful. The rooms, the food, the lobby, the beach, pools, activities. We loved it all. We were pampered from the moment we walked in with the champagne and cold towels. We were there the weekend of the Mayweather-Pacquiao fight and Dreams planned a fight event where everyone could watch it on 3 large screens. None of my guests wanted to miss the fight and it gave them something to do Saturday night after dinner so it was perfect. There were a lot of special touches, excellent service, and other great things that made me feel great about our choice in Dreams. I did not have the privilege to do the site visit beforehand, but I can say it was better in person than all the pictures and reviews I obsessed over for months. <\/span><\/span><\/p>\n<p>\u00a0<\/p>\n<p><strong><span  style=\"font-family:arial, sans-serif\"><span  style=\"font-size:9pt\">Room:<\/span><\/span><\/strong><span  style=\"font-family:arial, sans-serif\"><span  style=\"font-size:9pt\"> A+ --Me and my mom booked the Preferred Club Master Suite. Then, my husband stayed there wedding night. (he stayed in an ocean view room for the nights before the wedding\u2014I\u2019m super traditional <\/span><\/span><span  style=\"font-family:wingdings\"><span  style=\"font-size:9pt\">J<\/span><\/span><span  style=\"font-family:arial, sans-serif\"><span  style=\"font-size:9pt\">). Ladies, the Master Suite was expensive yes BUT, I am so happy we booked it. We used the value of the free rooms (book 5 get a 6<sup>th<\/sup> free) we received to pay for it. On Friday night, my bridesmaids threw me a bachelorette party in our room before going out and with all 20 girls playing games, we definitely needed the space. Also, on our wedding day, with the photographers, videographers, my 4 bridesmaids, my mom, my backup makeup artist, my hair stylist \u2013 we really needed the space! I felt so comfortable. Plus, having that amazing view for the weekend was great, and I really think I deserved it after all the planning and stress!<\/span><\/span><\/p>\n<p>\u00a0<\/p>\n<p><strong><span  style=\"font-family:arial, sans-serif\"><span  style=\"font-size:9pt\">Rehearsal:<\/span><\/span><\/strong><span  style=\"font-family:arial, sans-serif\"><span  style=\"font-size:9pt\"> Our rehearsal was scheduled at 10am Saturday morning. I was on time and so was my coordinator but we were missing the GROOM and half of the wedding party. My wedding coordinator asked could we move it to 11 when they still were not there by 10:10. Had my first (and only, thankfully) bridezilla moment because I was furious that they were not on time. But so thankful my WC was available for reschedule. I blamed it on our crazy partying in Cancun the night before and asked them to please be on time for the rest of the wedding events. <\/span><\/span><\/p>\n<p>\u00a0<\/p>\n<p><strong><span  style=\"font-family:arial, sans-serif\"><span  style=\"font-size:9pt\">Welcome Reception:<\/span><\/span><\/strong><span  style=\"font-family:arial, sans-serif\"><span  style=\"font-size:9pt\"> We had our welcome reception Friday at 7pm at the North Jacuzzi. I had my guests all wear white and it turned out PERFECTLY. Elisa surprised me with lighting and signature drinks which matched my wedding colors called Purple Rain. She\u2019s such a doll. We handed out our welcome bags at the welcome reception and everyone mixed and mingled. <\/span><\/span><span  style=\"font-family:wingdings\"><span  style=\"font-size:9pt\">J<\/span><\/span><span  style=\"font-family:arial, sans-serif\"><span  style=\"font-size:9pt\"> Appetizers: <span  style=\"color:rgb(40,40,40)\">roasted pepper and parmesan panini, shrimp satay, stuffed mushrooms, fish croquette, and spring rolls<\/span><\/span><\/span><\/p>\n<p>\u00a0<\/p>\n<p><strong><span  style=\"font-family:arial, sans-serif\"><span  style=\"font-size:9pt\">Flowers:<\/span><\/span><\/strong><span  style=\"font-family:arial, sans-serif\"><span  style=\"font-size:9pt\"> I love flowers and was insistent that there will be absolutely no fake flowers at my wedding and I\u2019m so happy with the result. Loved my cascading bouquet and my bridesmaid\u2019s bouquets, our centerpieces and the flower vases at the ceremony. I had fuchsia roses, purple orchids and purple lisianthus. Beautiful and vibrant colors just like I wanted.<\/span><\/span><\/p>\n<p>\u00a0<\/p>\n<p><strong><span  style=\"font-family:arial, sans-serif\"><span  style=\"font-size:9pt\">Wedding Ceremony:<\/span><\/span><\/strong><span  style=\"font-family:arial, sans-serif\"><span  style=\"font-size:9pt\"> We had the symbolic ceremony at the gazebo at 5pm Sunday, May 3, 2015. I had been so nervous about it being so close to the pool and the onlookers but I did not notice anyone but my guests and groom. Now, looking at the pictures from my guests, I see there were a LOT of people watching from the pool and their balconies. Thankfully my photographers did not capture them in a lot of the pictures. It was BEAUTIFUL. I did not want to get married on sand because I love wearing heels and knew my now husband wanted to wear shoes too. Overlooking the ocean was just absolutely breathtaking. Elisa surprised me with the chandelier and drapery which looked amazing. Everything we had went over, from the flower vases, rose petals in aisle, chair sashes tied on the silver tiffany chairs, fans, reserved seating name tags \u2013 was executed perfectly. Better than I imagined. I love how all our pictures look and it felt magical. Our officiant was Luis Armando\u00a0Sanchez\u00a0Navarrete. I met with him on Saturday to go over the script I wrote and our name pronunciations. Very sweet man. Also very gracious, considering I was late for our appointment the day before. He did great but I will say I could not understand about 20% of the ceremony due to his heavy accent, but it was totally fine <\/span><\/span><span  style=\"font-family:wingdings\"><span  style=\"font-size:9pt\">J<\/span><\/span><span  style=\"font-family:arial, sans-serif\"><span  style=\"font-size:9pt\"> I completely customized the ceremony script, did not have a sand ceremony, and we said our own vows. It was a very sweet ceremony.<\/span><\/span><\/p>\n<p>\u00a0<\/p>\n<p><strong><span  style=\"font-family:arial, sans-serif\"><span  style=\"font-size:9pt\">Informal Cocktail Hour:<\/span><\/span><\/strong><span  style=\"font-family:arial, sans-serif\"><span  style=\"font-size:9pt\"> We opted to use the money included in the package for the 20 guests for the cocktail hour to extend our reception by 1 hour. So happy we did this. Our guests went to the lobby bar while we took pictures and it turned out great. <\/span><\/span><\/p>\n<p>\u00a0<\/p>\n<p><strong><span  style=\"font-family:arial, sans-serif\"><span  style=\"font-size:9pt\">Wedding Reception:<\/span><\/span><\/strong><span  style=\"font-family:arial, sans-serif\"><span  style=\"font-size:9pt\"> MY FAVE. Our reception was on the pool deck from 7pm-11pm. I had 2 long empire tables and we sat at the sweetheart table. I upgraded the tablecloths to purple satin and our sweetheart table cloth to silver sequin. We also upgraded to the love seat for our sweetheart table. We had several beautiful flower arrangements, tall glass vases with floating candles, votive candle holders (with LED lights<\/span><\/span><span  style=\"font-family:wingdings\"><span  style=\"font-size:9pt\">J<\/span><\/span><span  style=\"font-family:arial, sans-serif\"><span  style=\"font-size:9pt\">), and mirrors under the vases down the center of each long empire table. I had exact seating arrangements, with a name tag on each maraca (which also tripled as our wedding favor and exit) that was placed directly on their napkin. For lighting, we had 2 strings of 20 floating lanterns. The bridal party entered the reception to Treasure by Bruno Mars. We then had our first dance to our guests holding sparklers, which I loveddddddddd. They only lasted a couple minutes but it was fine because we got great pictures and video while they did last. We had a combination of all the buffets, it was delicious. My guests said it was the best they had all weekend. We had the marble cake with orchids decorating and brought our own cake topper. For our guest book, we had a Polaroid camera where guests could take pictures with props and then sign a message under their picture. We made our own dinner playlist using our favorite love songs on Spotify. I did not want to rent the DJ because I did not think he would play all the songs we wanted, so we just had a mix made by a local DJ that we played through our iPad. We did not rent a dance floor but instead danced directly on the deck. We partied!!!!! My guests are so much fun and we didn\u2019t sit down the entire reception. We exited to everyone shaking their maracas and we danced down the middle. PERFECTION. Buffet: pasta salad, mixed greens with vegetables, chicken caesar salad, potato salad with scallions, homemade bread and rolls, seafood salad, cajun roasted potatoes, creole pasta, corn on the cob, chicken breast stuffed with spinach, seafood casserole, jamaican chicken, cajun beef brochettes, seafood paella, BBQ pork ribs, coconut and rum cake, brownies, carrot cake, apple strudel<\/span><\/span><\/p>\n<p><strong><span  style=\"font-family:arial, sans-serif\"><span  style=\"font-size:9pt\">After the wedding reception:<\/span><\/span><\/strong><span  style=\"font-family:arial, sans-serif\"><span  style=\"font-size:9pt\"> Never ever ever thought I would be a bride to continue partying with the guests after the reception was over but we really didn\u2019t want the night to end. I changed out of my dress into a cute little white outfit (had to stay looking bridal haha) and we headed down to the Desires Nightclub until 1am. We had SO MUCH FUN. And the DJ played whatever we wanted. It was perfect.<\/span><\/span><\/p>\n<p>\u00a0<\/p>\n<p><strong><span  style=\"font-family:arial, sans-serif\"><span  style=\"font-size:9pt\">Farewell Brunch:<\/span><\/span><\/strong><span  style=\"font-family:arial, sans-serif\"><span  style=\"font-size:9pt\"> Most of our guests were leaving Monday so we had an informal brunch at the World Caf\u00e9 9:30am-11am. Mostly everyone came and some of our guests had gotten there early to save us a few tables. It was so great to hug and kiss everyone goodbye before we went to our amazing honeymoon (at Excellence Playa Mujeres \u2013 separate review on Trip Advisor). <\/span><\/span><\/p>\n<p>\u00a0<\/p>\n<p><strong><span  style=\"font-family:arial, sans-serif\"><span  style=\"font-size:9pt\">Photographer\/Videographer:<\/span><\/span><\/strong><span  style=\"font-family:arial, sans-serif\"><span  style=\"font-size:9pt\"> B --Digital Cinema. So I did not have a lot of money for photography. I knew I wouldn\u2019t be spending the $5k plus like other brides even though I LOVE pictures. Thankfully, I found these guys by searching the #dreamsrivieracancun hashtag on Instagram and finding this beautiful brides pictures. I LOVE my pictures and love my highlight video. The communication was great at first, sometimes lacking but in the end I got a great price. I believe because of the language barriers, at times I do not think they understood some of my requests \u2013 specifically, about a week before my wedding I decided to extend my reception to 11pm instead of 10pm. I emailed them to ask the price to extend the reception to 11, they said $100, I said great let\u2019s do it, they said okay and also they will arrive at 3 instead of 4 (my ceremony started at 5). Fast forward to 10pm at my reception, they said they are leaving because they got there at 3 and that was the amount of hours we agreed on in our initial contract.\u00a0 I was really upset for a few moments because I knew for a fact I was very specific in my emails but then decided not to argue with them. And plus I didn\u2019t have my phone to pull up my email to prove we agreed they were supposed to leave at 11 so I just let it go and decided to enjoy the rest of my reception. The only thing they didn\u2019t capture was the maraca exit but thankfully I have other footage of that. There were a few other issues of things I thought I should have received based on the contract, and I\u2019m still waiting to see if I will :\/ Also, there are shots I wish I would have gotten but I do love all the pics and video that we did receive so I\u2019m not going stress out about it.<\/span><\/span><\/p>\n<p>\u00a0<\/p>\n<p><strong><span  style=\"font-family:arial, sans-serif\"><span  style=\"font-size:9pt\">Wedding Favors:<\/span><\/span><\/strong><span  style=\"font-family:arial, sans-serif\"><span  style=\"font-size:9pt\"> A --We ordered our personalized authentic maracas from Maracas Mexico. Communication was great and timely. The maracas were pretty and they were at the resort when I arrived. I ordered the original multicolor design and requested as many purple maracas as possible, which they agreed to. The only \u201ccomplaint\u201d I have is that I didn\u2019t receive not 1 purple maraca! But it actually turned out fine, it didn\u2019t matter <\/span><\/span><span  style=\"font-family:wingdings\"><span  style=\"font-size:9pt\">J<\/span><\/span><\/p>\n<p>\u00a0<\/p>\n<p><strong><span  style=\"font-family:arial, sans-serif\"><span  style=\"font-size:9pt\">Welcome Bags:<\/span><\/span><\/strong><span  style=\"font-family:arial, sans-serif\"><span  style=\"font-size:9pt\"> I had paper welcome bags that I gave to everyone at our welcome reception that included tumblers from DollarTree with personalized stickers from Davet Designs, advil, hand sanitizer, bug repellent wipes, maraca keychains, welcome letter\/itinerary\/meet-the-guests booklet, and sunscreen. Only a few people used the tumblers, and even me and my now husband didn\u2019t use them because I would forget to take them down with us to the beach\/pool everyday lol. But oh well, it was another take home gift for our guests <\/span><\/span><span  style=\"font-family:wingdings\"><span  style=\"font-size:9pt\">J<\/span><\/span><span  style=\"font-family:arial, sans-serif\"><span  style=\"font-size:9pt\"> People did love our booklets and said they used the advil, especially after our night partying in Cancun on Friday.<\/span><\/span><\/p>\n<p>\u00a0<\/p>\n<p><strong><span  style=\"font-family:arial, sans-serif\"><span  style=\"font-size:9pt\">Makeup:<\/span><\/span><\/strong><span  style=\"font-family:arial, sans-serif\"><span  style=\"font-size:9pt\"> A --I had my makeup done at the spa at the resort by Concepcion. I was very nervous about the makeup so I bought all the makeup beforehand for my dream look and had my girls ready just in case I hated what the makeup lady did. Concepcion did AMAZING. I was very happy and I\u2019m very picky lol. She used all MAC products. She did use my foundation because I wanted a perfect match. She didn\u2019t have the exact lip color I wanted so I used my own lipstain\/gloss and polish that I brought. Very satisfied. As a side note, lashes are an additional $15 but I brought my own and had my friend put them on for me.<\/span><\/span><\/p>\n<p>\u00a0<\/p>\n<p><strong><span  style=\"font-family:arial, sans-serif\"><span  style=\"font-size:9pt\">Hair:<\/span><\/span><\/strong><span  style=\"font-family:arial, sans-serif\"><span  style=\"font-size:9pt\"> I brought my own stylist.<\/span><\/span><\/p>\n<p>\u00a0<\/p>\n<p><span  style=\"font-family:arial, sans-serif\"><span  style=\"font-size:9pt\">All in all, I HAD THE ABSOLUTE WEDDING OF MY DREAMS. I would not change a thing. A lot of my guests said it\u2019s the best wedding they have ever been to, and seeing all their smiles in the pictures and videos, makes me feel very happy. It was worth all the money and stress! Best day of my life. Complete fairytale.<\/span><\/span><\/p>\n<p>\u00a0<\/p>\n<p><a href='https:\/\/vimeo.com\/128508480' class='bbc_url' title='External link' rel='nofollow external'>https:\/\/<span>vimeo<...>.com\/128508480<\/a><\/p>\n<p>\u00a0<\/p>\n<p><a class='resized_img' rel='lightbox[1897167]' id='ipb-attach-url-' href=\"http:\/\/bdw.stevewright.netdna-cdn.com\/cdn\/monthly_05_2015\/post-277044-0-70558000-1432530687.png\" title=\"bags.png - Size: 467.38KB\"><img itemprop=\"image\" src=\"http:\/\/bdw.stevewright.netdna-cdn.com\/cdn\/monthly_05_2015\/post-277044-0-70558000-1432530687.png\" class='bbc_img linked-image' alt=\"bags.png\" \/><\/a>\n\n<a class='resized_img' rel='lightbox[1897167]' id='ipb-attach-url-' href=\"http:\/\/bdw.stevewright.netdna-cdn.com\/cdn\/monthly_05_2015\/post-277044-0-09192600-1432530696.png\" title=\"group1.png - Size: 919.64KB\"><img itemprop=\"image\" src=\"http:\/\/bdw.stevewright.netdna-cdn.com\/cdn\/monthly_05_2015\/post-277044-0-09192600-1432530696.png\" class='bbc_img linked-image' alt=\"group1.png\" \/><\/a>\n\n<a class='resized_img' rel='lightbox[1897167]' id='ipb-attach-url-' href=\"http:\/\/bdw.stevewright.netdna-cdn.com\/cdn\/monthly_05_2015\/post-277044-0-73651900-1432530704.png\" title=\"purple rain.png - Size: 1.03MB\"><img itemprop=\"image\" src=\"http:\/\/bdw.stevewright.netdna-cdn.com\/cdn\/monthly_05_2015\/post-277044-0-73651900-1432530704.png\" class='bbc_img linked-image' alt=\"purple rain.png\" \/><\/a>\n\n<a class='resized_img' rel='lightbox[1897167]' id='ipb-attach-url-' href=\"http:\/\/bdw.stevewright.netdna-cdn.com\/cdn\/monthly_05_2015\/post-277044-0-66031100-1432530708.png\" title=\"selfies.png - Size: 420.51KB\"><img itemprop=\"image\" src=\"http:\/\/bdw.stevewright.netdna-cdn.com\/cdn\/monthly_05_2015\/post-277044-0-66031100-1432530708.png\" class='bbc_img linked-image' alt=\"selfies.png\" \/><\/a>\n\n<a class='resized_img' rel='lightbox[1897167]' id='ipb-attach-url-' href=\"http:\/\/bdw.stevewright.netdna-cdn.com\/cdn\/monthly_05_2015\/post-277044-0-61440900-1432530711.png\" title=\"us1.png - Size: 316.36KB\"><img itemprop=\"image\" src=\"http:\/\/bdw.stevewright.netdna-cdn.com\/cdn\/monthly_05_2015\/post-277044-0-61440900-1432530711.png\" class='bbc_img linked-image' alt=\"us1.png\" \/><\/a>\n\n<a class='resized_img' rel='lightbox[1897167]' id='ipb-attach-url-' href=\"http:\/\/bdw.stevewright.netdna-cdn.com\/cdn\/monthly_05_2015\/post-277044-0-10106800-1432530763.png\" title=\"dress.png - Size: 804.98KB\"><img itemprop=\"image\" src=\"http:\/\/bdw.stevewright.netdna-cdn.com\/cdn\/monthly_05_2015\/post-277044-0-10106800-1432530763.png\" class='bbc_img linked-image' alt=\"dress.png\" \/><\/a>\n\n<a class='resized_img' rel='lightbox[1897167]' id='ipb-attach-url-' href=\"http:\/\/bdw.stevewright.netdna-cdn.com\/cdn\/monthly_05_2015\/post-277044-0-39449500-1432530775.png\" title=\"bouquets.png - Size: 959.27KB\"><img itemprop=\"image\" src=\"http:\/\/bdw.stevewright.netdna-cdn.com\/cdn\/monthly_05_2015\/post-277044-0-39449500-1432530775.png\" class='bbc_img linked-image' alt=\"bouquets.png\" \/><\/a>\n\n<a class='resized_img' rel='lightbox[1897167]' id='ipb-attach-url-' href=\"http:\/\/bdw.stevewright.netdna-cdn.com\/cdn\/monthly_05_2015\/post-277044-0-59558100-1432530789.png\" title=\"robes.png - Size: 969.83KB\"><img itemprop=\"image\" src=\"http:\/\/bdw.stevewright.netdna-cdn.com\/cdn\/monthly_05_2015\/post-277044-0-59558100-1432530789.png\" class='bbc_img linked-image' alt=\"robes.png\" \/><\/a>\n\n<a class='resized_img' rel='lightbox[1897167]' id='ipb-attach-url-' href=\"http:\/\/bdw.stevewright.netdna-cdn.com\/cdn\/monthly_05_2015\/post-277044-0-37332100-1432530800.png\" title=\"before.png - Size: 705.24KB\"><img itemprop=\"image\" src=\"http:\/\/bdw.stevewright.netdna-cdn.com\/cdn\/monthly_05_2015\/post-277044-0-37332100-1432530800.png\" class='bbc_img linked-image' alt=\"before.png\" \/><\/a>\n\n<a class='resized_img' rel='lightbox[1897167]' id='ipb-attach-url-' href=\"http:\/\/bdw.stevewright.netdna-cdn.com\/cdn\/monthly_05_2015\/post-277044-0-69954900-1432530817.png\" title=\"all on the way.png - Size: 1.16MB\"><img itemprop=\"image\" src=\"http:\/\/bdw.stevewright.netdna-cdn.com\/cdn\/monthly_05_2015\/post-277044-0-69954900-1432530817.png\" class='bbc_img linked-image' alt=\"all on the way.png\" \/><\/a>\n\n<a class='resized_img' rel='lightbox[1897167]' id='ipb-attach-url-' href=\"http:\/\/bdw.stevewright.netdna-cdn.com\/cdn\/monthly_05_2015\/post-277044-0-13525200-1432530835.png\" title=\"aisle.png - Size: 1.27MB\"><img itemprop=\"image\" src=\"http:\/\/bdw.stevewright.netdna-cdn.com\/cdn\/monthly_05_2015\/post-277044-0-13525200-1432530835.png\" class='bbc_img linked-image' alt=\"aisle.png\" \/><\/a>\n\n<a class='resized_img' rel='lightbox[1897167]' id='ipb-attach-url-' href=\"http:\/\/bdw.stevewright.netdna-cdn.com\/cdn\/monthly_05_2015\/post-277044-0-19385600-1432530851.png\" title=\"aisle4.png - Size: 1.21MB\"><img itemprop=\"image\" src=\"http:\/\/bdw.stevewright.netdna-cdn.com\/cdn\/monthly_05_2015\/post-277044-0-19385600-1432530851.png\" class='bbc_img linked-image' alt=\"aisle4.png\" \/><\/a>\n\n<a class='resized_img' rel='lightbox[1897167]' id='ipb-attach-url-' href=\"http:\/\/bdw.stevewright.netdna-cdn.com\/cdn\/monthly_05_2015\/post-277044-0-18841000-1432530865.png\" title=\"alter2.png - Size: 1.05MB\"><img itemprop=\"image\" src=\"http:\/\/bdw.stevewright.netdna-cdn.com\/cdn\/monthly_05_2015\/post-277044-0-18841000-1432530865.png\" class='bbc_img linked-image' alt=\"alter2.png\" \/><\/a>\n\n<a class='resized_img' rel='lightbox[1897167]' id='ipb-attach-url-' href=\"http:\/\/bdw.stevewright.netdna-cdn.com\/cdn\/monthly_05_2015\/post-277044-0-77730900-1432530879.png\" title=\"alter5.png - Size: 1.11MB\"><img itemprop=\"image\" src=\"http:\/\/bdw.stevewright.netdna-cdn.com\/cdn\/monthly_05_2015\/post-277044-0-77730900-1432530879.png\" class='bbc_img linked-image' alt=\"alter5.png\" \/><\/a>\n\n<a class='resized_img' rel='lightbox[1897167]' id='ipb-attach-url-' href=\"http:\/\/bdw.stevewright.netdna-cdn.com\/cdn\/monthly_05_2015\/post-277044-0-85504100-1432530895.png\" title=\"alter9.png - Size: 1.1MB\"><img itemprop=\"image\" src=\"http:\/\/bdw.stevewright.netdna-cdn.com\/cdn\/monthly_05_2015\/post-277044-0-85504100-1432530895.png\" class='bbc_img linked-image' alt=\"alter9.png\" \/><\/a>\n\n<a class='resized_img' rel='lightbox[1897167]' id='ipb-attach-url-' href=\"http:\/\/bdw.stevewright.netdna-cdn.com\/cdn\/monthly_05_2015\/post-277044-0-74966800-1432530956.png\" title=\"alter16.png - Size: 744.15KB\"><img itemprop=\"image\" src=\"http:\/\/bdw.stevewright.netdna-cdn.com\/cdn\/monthly_05_2015\/post-277044-0-74966800-1432530956.png\" class='bbc_img linked-image' alt=\"alter16.png\" \/><\/a>\n\n<a class='resized_img' rel='lightbox[1897167]' id='ipb-attach-url-' href=\"http:\/\/bdw.stevewright.netdna-cdn.com\/cdn\/monthly_05_2015\/post-277044-0-71426800-1432530968.png\" title=\"alter28.png - Size: 1.03MB\"><img itemprop=\"image\" src=\"http:\/\/bdw.stevewright.netdna-cdn.com\/cdn\/monthly_05_2015\/post-277044-0-71426800-1432530968.png\" class='bbc_img linked-image' alt=\"alter28.png\" \/><\/a>\n\n<a class='resized_img' rel='lightbox[1897167]' id='ipb-attach-url-' href=\"http:\/\/bdw.stevewright.netdna-cdn.com\/cdn\/monthly_05_2015\/post-277044-0-52576800-1432530985.png\" title=\"group.png - Size: 1.2MB\"><img itemprop=\"image\" src=\"http:\/\/bdw.stevewright.netdna-cdn.com\/cdn\/monthly_05_2015\/post-277044-0-52576800-1432530985.png\" class='bbc_img linked-image' alt=\"group.png\" \/><\/a>\n\n<a class='resized_img' rel='lightbox[1897167]' id='ipb-attach-url-' href=\"http:\/\/bdw.stevewright.netdna-cdn.com\/cdn\/monthly_05_2015\/post-277044-0-10115800-1432531001.png\" title=\"bridalpartyalter1.png - Size: 1.15MB\"><img itemprop=\"image\" src=\"http:\/\/bdw.stevewright.netdna-cdn.com\/cdn\/monthly_05_2015\/post-277044-0-10115800-1432531001.png\" class='bbc_img linked-image' alt=\"bridalpartyalter1.png\" \/><\/a>\n\n<a class='resized_img' rel='lightbox[1897167]' id='ipb-attach-url-' href=\"http:\/\/bdw.stevewright.netdna-cdn.com\/cdn\/monthly_05_2015\/post-277044-0-13253200-1432531015.png\" title=\"bridalpartybeach.png - Size: 1.06MB\"><img itemprop=\"image\" src=\"http:\/\/bdw.stevewright.netdna-cdn.com\/cdn\/monthly_05_2015\/post-277044-0-13253200-1432531015.png\" class='bbc_img linked-image' alt=\"bridalpartybeach.png\" \/><\/a>\n\n<a class='resized_img' rel='lightbox[1897167]' id='ipb-attach-url-' href=\"http:\/\/bdw.stevewright.netdna-cdn.com\/cdn\/monthly_05_2015\/post-277044-0-44608800-1432531027.png\" title=\"usbeach4.png - Size: 992.91KB\"><img itemprop=\"image\" src=\"http:\/\/bdw.stevewright.netdna-cdn.com\/cdn\/monthly_05_2015\/post-277044-0-44608800-1432531027.png\" class='bbc_img linked-image' alt=\"usbeach4.png\" \/><\/a>\n\n<a class='resized_img' rel='lightbox[1897167]' id='ipb-attach-url-' href=\"http:\/\/bdw.stevewright.netdna-cdn.com\/cdn\/monthly_05_2015\/post-277044-0-04673600-1432531039.png\" title=\"usbeach5.png - Size: 865.73KB\"><img itemprop=\"image\" src=\"http